  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ID: Indigenous Peoples Alliance for Rights and Development (IPARD)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Bureau for Inclusive Growth, Partnerships, and Innovation (IPI)):  The Indigenous Peoples&apos; Alliance for Rights and Development is a public-private partnership to secure rights, enhance capabilities, and create self-determined economic opportunities for Indigenous Peoples worldwide. This partnership harnesses the strengths and experiences of a collective, multi-sector network to empower Indigenous Peoples&apos; organizations and catalyze an enabling environment where Indigenous Peoples can manage, develop, and govern their own territories based on the principles of self-determined development, traditional practices, natural resource management, and respect for their customary rights.   This program contributes to the National Security Strategy and the Joint Strategic Plan by helping to create a prosperous world through supporting inclusive economic growth, supporting the dignity of individuals, empowering local actors to seek enduring solutions to their development challenges, and improving and adapting policy and foreign assistance to advance the inclusion of Indigenous peoples. This IM implements the Indigenous People directive/earmark.</narrative>
  </description>
